  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Age Statements and Timeline Models",
    "description": "Translate age statements into equations by anchoring everyone’s age to the same present, past, or future date.",
    "teachingApproach": "Use short, connected phone-sized teaching screens with concrete ages, labelled dates, separate calculation lines, a reason for each step, and an original-clue check. Place a fresh matching practice question after each worked example; wrong answers receive a worked correction and parallel practice.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 26,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 8, Problems on Ages. Approved scope: Teach a stable variable model for age problems: choose present ages as variables or express another person’s age relative to one variable, then shift every person's age by the same number of years for a common past or future date. Translate phrases such as years ago, years hence, twice as old, one-third as old, and an age difference into equations. Explain that an age is attached to a person and a time; label each equation with its time anchor. Distinguish a person's age from an age ratio, which generally changes over time. Include a timeline/table, sign checks for past ages, and substitution in the original statement. Learners should turn prose into a consistent model without mixing dates or applying different time shifts to people in the same year."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn how ages change with time.\n\nAsha is 24 today. She was younger five years ago and will be older three years from now. Let's put those ages in order.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Picture Asha's age on a timeline:\n\n5 years ago: 19\nToday: 24\n3 years later: 27\n\nEach line is the same person at a different date.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Start at today, 24.\n\nLook back five years:\n24 − 5 = 19\n\nLook ahead three years:\n24 + 3 = 27\n\nPast means subtract. Future means add. Check by moving back: 27 − 3 = 24.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
