    "teach_4": {
      "id": "teach_4",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Age questions also compare two people.\n\n“P is twice Q's age” means:\nP = 2 × Q\n\n“P is one-third of Q's age” means:\nP = Q ÷ 3\n\nThese are multiplication and division, not a change of date.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_4_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_4_step": {
      "id": "teach_4_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "For example, Q is 18 today.\n\nTwice Q: 2 × 18 = 36\nOne-third of Q: 18 ÷ 3 = 6\n\nCheck the second statement: three groups of 6 make 18. Now try the same idea with a fresh age.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_4"
        }
      ]
    },
